  "_notes": "Reef extras (P4.1-P4.5), built by components/Extras and attached into the config/scene.json layer Groups by id. Positions are design pixels (1920x1080 inside the camera Group) from docs/art/placement-proposal.json. current is the one shared water current: every sway chain loops over current.period x art.periodScale seconds, with its phase taken from its base x (one wave of waveLength px travelling right) plus phaseDeg. chainArt: segments run base to tip; pivot is the segment's rotation point in its own pixels (the Poster is drawn at -pivot) and attach is where the next segment's pivot sits; amplitudeDeg is each segment's own swing (nested, so the tip sums them); lagSec delays each segment behind the one below. chains are free-standing sway chains: x, y is the base pivot. anemone: body and tentacle chains go in anemone.layer (the front lane) so the hosted clownfish draws between them: the body and the critters are inserted behind the lane's FishBrain and the tentacles after it. anemone.host is read by FishBrain (components/lib/host.brs): fish of host.species in host.lane start nestling within radius px of (x, y), roam out to leash px and return. critters walk seeded loops along y (top-left of the sprite, so the feet sit on the ground) between left and right (components/lib/extras.brs extrasWalkPath); the shrimp turns by switching between its pre-mirrored r and l art. ripple: copies of a 1920-wide strip side by side from x0, scrolled left by one strip width per periodSec plus a +-bobPx vertical bob, tinted day..night; periodSec and bobSec must divide 45 s of scene time, so tests/visual/drift.spec.ts, which compares the surface band half a drift period (45 s) apart, stays drift-only. caustics: tiles in a clipped Group over the sand band; each tile layer scrolls one tile along dir per periodSec. Night: the Extras nightLevel field (0 day, 1 night) fades the caustics (hidden from hideAt) and moves the ripple tint/opacity from day to night. Colours are 0xRRGGBBAA strings.",
